    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64267" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λύτρ-ωσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ransoming</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰχμαλώτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Arat.</u>
					11
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Le.</u>
				25.29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
				1.68
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Hebr.</u>
				9.12
			</span></i>; <i>redemption</i> of a pledge, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PTeb.</u>
				120.41
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A. D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>release, discharge</i> from an obligation, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1130.20
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(v A. D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. ὕδατος</span>, =
			<i>spring</i> of water, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Jd.</u>
				1.15
			</span></i>.</div>
